# {{project_name}}

Agentforce BYOC Function created with the Agentforce SDK.

## Overview

This is a BYOC (Bring Your Own Code) function that can be deployed to Salesforce and executed within Agentforce workflows. Functions are defined using decorators for schema validation and can be tested locally or deployed to Salesforce.

## Project Structure

```
{{project_name}}/
├── main.py               # Your function implementation with decorators
├── entry_func.py         # Schema decorator utilities (entry point)
├── schema.py             # Schema decorators (request/response)
├── agentforce_byoc/      # Vendored SDK (until it's published to PyPI)
├── config.json           # Function configuration (entryPoint)
├── Dockerfile            # Container definition for deployment
├── pyproject.toml        # Python dependencies (Poetry)
├── .python-version       # Python 3.11
├── .gitignore            # Git ignore patterns
├── .dockerignore         # Docker ignore patterns
├── Makefile              # Development tasks
└── README.md             # This file
```

> `agentforce_byoc/` is a copy of the SDK runtime, vendored by `agentforce init`
> because the SDK isn't on PyPI yet. It's what lets your deployed package
> `import agentforce_byoc`. When the SDK is published, this directory goes away
> and it becomes a normal dependency.

## Quick Start

### 1. Install Dependencies

```bash
poetry install
```

### 2. Test Locally

Set your credentials, then run the agent against the Agentforce BYOC runtime:

```bash
export ORG_JWT_TOKEN=<org-jwt>
export SFDC_CORE_TENANT_ID=core/<instance>-<fd>/<org-id>
export SFDC_USER_ID=<user-id>
export SFDC_APP_CONTEXT=<app-context>
agentforce run main.py
```

### 3. Implement Your Function

Edit `main.py` and define your schemas:

```python
# TODO: Define your function schemas here
class MyRequest(TypedDict):
    input_text: str
    max_length: int

class MyResponse(TypedDict):
    output_text: str
    status: str

@entry_func
@requestSchema(MyRequest)
@responseSchema(MyResponse)
def function(request: dict) -> dict:
    # Your implementation
    return {"output_text": "result", "status": "success"}
