## Troubleshooting

### Function fails locally

1. Check Python version: `python --version` (should be 3.11+)
2. Install dependencies: `poetry install`
3. Check imports in `main.py`
4. Verify `ORG_JWT_TOKEN`, `SFDC_CORE_TENANT_ID`, `SFDC_USER_ID`, and `SFDC_APP_CONTEXT` are exported

### Agentforce BYOC runtime fails

1. Check `ORG_JWT_TOKEN` is set: `echo $ORG_JWT_TOKEN`
2. Verify the JWT is valid and not expired
3. Check `SFDC_CORE_TENANT_ID` is set and well-formed (core/<instance>-<fd>/<org-id>)
4. Check `SFDC_USER_ID` is set (relay sends it as `x-sfdc-user-id`)
5. Check `SFDC_APP_CONTEXT` is set (relay sends it as `x-sfdc-app-context`)

### Deployment fails

1. Verify `ORG_JWT_TOKEN`, `SFDC_CORE_TENANT_ID`, `SFDC_USER_ID`, and `SFDC_APP_CONTEXT` env vars are set (commands abort if unset)
2. Check the JWT is valid and not expired
3. Check package structure: `tar -tzf {{project_name}}-*.tar.gz`

## CLI Command Reference

```bash
# Initialize new function
agentforce init <name>

# Run locally (requires ORG_JWT_TOKEN + SFDC_CORE_TENANT_ID + SFDC_USER_ID + SFDC_APP_CONTEXT)
agentforce run main.py

# Package for deployment
agentforce zip .
agentforce zip . --output custom-name.tar.gz

# Build end-to-end (validate -> run -> zip)
agentforce package .

# Deploy to Agentforce BYOC (set ORG_JWT_TOKEN + SFDC_CORE_TENANT_ID + SFDC_USER_ID + SFDC_APP_CONTEXT env vars first)
agentforce deploy --package-name <name> --package-file <name>-0.1.0.tar.gz
agentforce deploy-status --package-name <name> --version 1.0

# Get help
agentforce --help
agentforce run --help
```

